    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is the last two digits of the registration-date year, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field with `@Column(name = \"membership_number\")` plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to all four `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` files (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically onto the response.\n\n4. **New step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` reads the built owner via `@Val`, computes `YY = registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (zero-padded), and sets `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY`, mutating the entity in place.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignMembershipNumber` step (under the `transaction` governance) between `assignCustomerCode` (which sets `customerCode`) and `assignHousehold`, so both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already populated when it runs.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
