        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` step is a faithful sibling of the existing `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`: same package, same `service(@Val Owner)` in-place-mutation pattern, same javadoc style documenting ordering dependencies, and the same `Locale.ROOT` formatting discipline. The logic sits in the right unit \u2014 a single small function class for a single derived field \u2014 matching the codebase's one-step-per-concern convention rather than being folded into `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` (which would have made that class a catch-all for two independent derivations).\n\nWiring is placed correctly in the pipeline: after `assignCustomerCode` (which it reads via `getCustomerCode()`) and after `BuildOwner` set the registration date, before `assignHousehold`/`SaveOwner`, and it carries the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors. Supporting changes are consistent and complete \u2014 getter/setter and `@Column` on the entity, the `membership_number` column across all four DB schemas, and a `readOnly` documented field in `openapi.yml` mirroring the `customerCode` entry. A maintainer of this repo would find this entirely natural; nothing is duplicated or misplaced."
